<section class="section comparison-section" id="compare">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="comparison-header reveal">
      <div class="label">Choose the right workflow</div>
      <h2 class="sec-title">WP Flame complements tools that solve different parts of performance work.</h2>
      <p class="sec-desc">The useful question is not which logo wins a checklist. It is which evidence and operating model fit the incident in front of you.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="comparison-grid">
      <article class="comparison-card reveal">
        <span>Current-request debugging</span>
        <h3>Query Monitor</h3>
        <p class="strength"><strong>Strong at:</strong> rich developer inspection of the current WordPress request.</p>
        <p><strong>WP Flame's intended difference:</strong> bounded retained evidence, guided diagnosis, capability reporting, compatible before/after work, and agency handoff.</p>
        <a href="/compare/query-monitor/">Read the balanced comparison →</a>
      </article>
      <article class="comparison-card reveal">
        <span>Infrastructure observability</span>
        <h3>Generic APM</h3>
        <p class="strength"><strong>Strong at:</strong> broader infrastructure visibility and, in some products, deeper PHP instrumentation.</p>
        <p><strong>WP Flame's intended difference:</strong> low-friction WordPress semantics without requiring a particular host or server agent.</p>
        <a href="/compare/generic-apm/">Read the balanced comparison →</a>
      </article>
      <article class="comparison-card reveal">
        <span>Public-page acceleration</span>
        <h3>Cache plugins</h3>
        <p class="strength"><strong>Strong at:</strong> bypassing PHP for eligible public requests and improving delivery.</p>
        <p><strong>WP Flame's intended difference:</strong> diagnosing dynamic requests that still execute WordPress, including checkout, admin, APIs, and background work.</p>
        <a href="/compare/cache-plugin/">Read the balanced comparison →</a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

